hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27570","Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Hilal, meaning Ibn Khabbab, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that Dubaaah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to perform Hajj and stipulate. He said: Yes. She said: How shall I say? He said: Say: Labbayk, O Allah, Labbayk; my release from ihram is from the land where You detain me."
"27571","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to me, from Usamah ibn Zayd, and Ali ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Fadl ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Dubaaah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that she slaughtered a sheep in her house, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to her: Feed us from your sheep. She said to the messenger: By Allah, nothing remains with us except the neck, and I am shy to send to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the neck. The messenger returned and informed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Return to her and say to her: Send it, for it guides and is the closest of the sheep to good and the farthest from harm."
